ed, kneeling, half-kneeling, squatting, crouching, bending, push-up, plank, or other active exercise posture, treat that person as NOT lying. Use visible support clues: buttocks plus legs for sitting; knees/shins for kneeling; flexed legs/feet under the pelvis for squatting; hands plus feet/knees actively elevating the torso for push-up/plank.\n3. Otherwise, return \"positive\" if a real person is clearly prone, supine, side-lying, horizontally collapsed, or curled in a genuine lying state, with substantial torso/back/chest/side/pelvis support from the floor, ground, road, corridor, industrial floor, or another abnormal non-rest surface.\n\nThe negative-posture check applies only when that stable posture is visibly clear. It must not veto a genuinely lying person merely because knees are bent, an arm touches the ground, or lying was intentional. Normal lying on a bed, sofa, or obvious rest support is negative. Mannequins, posters, and screen-only people are negative.\n\nReturn \"uncertain\" only when tiny scale, severe blur/occlusion, or unclear support relationships prevent a reliable visible-state decision. Do not use temporal reasoning or require video.\n\nIf any real person clearly meets the positive definition, the whole image is positive. Return exactly one JSON object and no additional text:\n\n{\n  \"person_fallen\": \"positive\",\n  \"evidence\": \"brief visible evidence\"\n}\n\nThe value of \"person_fallen\" must be exactly \"positive\", \"negative\", or \"uncertain\".\n","stream":false,"format":"json","think":false,"options":{"temperature":0,"num_ctx":8192,"num_predict":256}},"image_sha256":"30bae33ef6a87738d1ee9d7d6ce2d42944cd954b3f4062fd6de26355e168188b","timestamp_start_utc":"2026-08-26T15:16:05.880146+00:00","timestamp_end_utc":"2026-08-26T15:16:07.307011+00:00"}
